  "reply": "Done.\n\n- **slug.py**: rewrote `slugify` to lowercase, collapse every run of non-alphanumerics into a single `-`, trim leading/trailing `-`, and fall back to `\"item\"` when nothing remains — matching all four SPEC.md points.\n- **tests/test_slug.py**: kept the existing `test_words` and added regression tests for the documented edge cases: mixed separators/punctuation (`\"  Hello,   World!! \"` → `hello-world`), collapsed separator runs (`\"---A___B---\"` → `a-b`), and no-alphanumerics (`\"!!!\"` → `item`). Now 4 test methods, satisfying the ≥3 requirement in acceptance.py.\n\nSPEC.md and acceptance.py were left untouched. The implementation also covers the non-ASCII case implicitly (any character that isn't `a-z0-9` after lowercasing is treated as a separator), so acceptance's three asserts and the unittest run will pass.",
